# Contributing to M.O.B. (Motors on Boost)

Thank you for your interest in **M.O.B. (Motors on Boost)**.

## Closed Contribution Policy

Please note that **M.O.B. (Motors on Boost)** is developed and maintained strictly **in-house** by Gerard "Jamie" (Jagofr) Francis and **RvL // ROGUE**. 

To preserve code architecture, strict proprietary IP rights, and targeted technical design:

* **No Pull Requests**: Unsolicited pull requests, forks submitted for upstream merge, or external code patches will be closed without review.
* **No External Feature Additions**: Core physics, procedural traffic systems, shader pipelines, and audio synthesizers are built to internal milestone roadmaps.
* **No Contributor License Agreement**: We do not accept contributions under third-party copyright or dual-licensing arrangements.

---

## Feedback, Bugs & Defect Reports

While code contributions are closed, bug discovery and feedback are appreciated:

1. **Bug Reports**: If you experience rendering glitches, WebGL crashes, audio stuttering, or gamepad binding failures, please open an Issue using the standard bug report format.
2. **Reproduction Details**: Always include your browser name/version, OS platform, GPU hardware, and connected input controller when reporting hardware or rendering issues.
3. **Feature Ideas & Discussions**: Feel free to share gameplay impressions or feature wishlists in the GitHub Discussions tab.

---

## Intellectual Property Notice

Any ideas, suggestions, defect workarounds, or concepts submitted through Issues or Discussions are provided voluntarily with no expectation of compensation, confidentiality, or proprietary reservation. By submitting, you grant RvL // ROGUE an unrestricted, irrevocable right to implement those ideas within the project.